conclusion: "At 12 km, a 39.2% longer main battery range (26.63 km to 37.07 km with Spotting Aircraft + Gun Fire Control System Modification 2) shrinks vertical dispersion from 95.5 m to 78.2 m; horizontal is unchanged at 170.4 m. With sigma 2.1, half of the shells land within 31.3% of the ellipse (53.3 m by 29.9 m) and 72.4% within its inner half; a higher sigma packs more shells toward the aim point. Aiming Systems Modification 1 narrows both: horizontal 170.4 m to 158.5 m, vertical 95.5 m to 88.8 m. Among tier 10 battleships at 12 km (41 ranked, 0 out of reach), Yamato on base ranks 19 of 41 on horizontal dispersion, 37 on vertical and 14 on the radius holding half of the shells; the median is 170.4 m horizontal and 88.8 m vertical, the tightest horizontal is Conte Verde (115.8 m)."
